1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,435
Ravan locked Ram's mother in the sea?

2
00:00:03,435 --> 00:00:05,840
And that too before Ram was even born.

3
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:08,932
This story is going around on phones everywhere.

4
00:00:08,932 --> 00:00:10,650
But where is it actually written?

5
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:12,024
The answer is shocking.

6
00:00:12,024 --> 00:00:15,458
This story really is written in a Sanskrit text.

7
00:00:15,458 --> 00:00:17,176
It's called Ananda Ramayan.

8
00:00:17,176 --> 00:00:19,580
But that is not Valmiki's Ramayan.

9
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:21,513
So then the question comes up.

10
00:00:21,513 --> 00:00:24,219
Why is this story not found in Valmiki?

11
00:00:24,219 --> 00:00:28,471
And when was Ananda Ramayan written? The answer will surprise you,

12
00:00:28,471 --> 00:00:30,790
because the date is much later.

13
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:34,839
Come on, let's go step by step with proof. We'll start with the viral story,

14
00:00:34,839 --> 00:00:38,152
then the Sanskrit text, then the proof from under the ground.

15
00:00:38,152 --> 00:00:40,360
At every step, the label will be clear.

16
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:44,616
But first understand why this story has such a hold on people.

17
00:00:44,616 --> 00:00:48,871
Because it has Ravan's fear, Brahma's prophecy,

18
00:00:48,871 --> 00:00:51,850
and a hidden box in the middle of the sea.

19
00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:53,107
Let's begin with the text.

20
00:00:53,107 --> 00:00:57,296
This story appears in the Sara Kanda of Ananda Ramayan.

21
00:00:57,296 --> 00:01:01,485
A Kanda means a big section of the text, like a chapter of a book.

22
00:01:01,485 --> 00:01:03,580
Now listen to what is written.

23
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:06,310
In the story, Ravan asks Brahma,

24
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:10,210
who will cause my death? Brahma's answer is straight.

25
00:01:10,210 --> 00:01:14,110
The son of Kaushalya and Dasharath will become the cause of your death.

26
00:01:14,110 --> 00:01:18,325
Just think, a king like Ravan, and he is afraid. Of whom?

27
00:01:18,325 --> 00:01:21,774
Of a child who hasn't even been born yet.

28
00:01:21,774 --> 00:01:24,840
This very fear drives the whole story forward.

29
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:28,586
The text says Kaushalya was just about to get married.

30
00:01:28,586 --> 00:01:30,834
Right before that, Ravan arrives,

31
00:01:30,834 --> 00:01:34,581
and carries off the princess. Before the wedding,

32
00:01:34,581 --> 00:01:35,330
note that.

33
00:01:35,330 --> 00:01:36,993
Then Ravan doesn't kill her.

34
00:01:36,993 --> 00:01:40,320
He shuts Kaushalya in a wooden box.

35
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:43,980
And he places the box in the middle of the sea, on a deserted island.

36
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:48,032
An island means a piece of land surrounded by water. No road,

37
00:01:48,032 --> 00:01:51,716
no boat. Ravan thinks, the wedding won't happen at all,

38
00:01:51,716 --> 00:01:53,190
so how will there be a son?

39
00:01:53,190 --> 00:01:58,187
But here's the twist. King Dasharath sets out by the sea route.

40
00:01:58,187 --> 00:02:01,820
On the way, Ravan ambushes and attacks him.

41
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:05,000
Ambush means attacking suddenly from hiding.

42
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,602
Dasharath survives.

43
00:02:06,602 --> 00:02:10,606
Carried by the waves, he reaches that same deserted island.

44
00:02:10,606 --> 00:02:14,610
And there he finds that same sealed wooden box.

45
00:02:14,610 --> 00:02:18,944
The box opens, and Kaushalya is inside. And the scripture says,

46
00:02:18,944 --> 00:02:23,279
their Gandharva marriage takes place right inside the box.

47
00:02:23,279 --> 00:02:27,180
Gandharva marriage means a marriage by mutual consent, without a wedding procession.

48
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:31,144
Just think, the very marriage Ravan did everything to stop,

49
00:02:31,144 --> 00:02:33,667
took place in the box he made himself.

50
00:02:33,667 --> 00:02:36,910
This twist in the story is what hooks people.

51
00:02:36,910 --> 00:02:39,381
The story is great, no doubt about that.

52
00:02:39,381 --> 00:02:41,851
But the real question starts now.

53
00:02:41,851 --> 00:02:43,616
What exactly is this Ananda Ramayan,

54
00:02:43,616 --> 00:02:46,440
and why is this not in Valmiki's Ramayan?

55
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,647
Now let's turn to that Ramayan

56
00:02:48,647 --> 00:02:51,589
which is known by Valmiki's name.

57
00:02:51,589 --> 00:02:54,163
We will open the Bala Kanda and the Uttara Kanda,

58
00:02:54,163 --> 00:02:56,370
because the clue should be in these.

59
00:02:56,370 --> 00:03:00,316
Bala Kanda means the part about Ram's birth and childhood.

60
00:03:00,316 --> 00:03:02,684
If Kaushalya had been abducted,

61
00:03:02,684 --> 00:03:05,052
this would be the most fitting place for it.

62
00:03:05,052 --> 00:03:07,420
Abduction means taking someone away by force.

63
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:08,782
But scholars say

64
00:03:08,782 --> 00:03:12,867
this box story is simply not found in Valmiki's old Ramayan.

65
00:03:12,867 --> 00:03:15,590
No attack by Ravan, no island in the sea.

66
00:03:15,590 --> 00:03:18,427
In the Bala Kanda, Dasharath is already king,

67
00:03:18,427 --> 00:03:21,974
and Kaushalya is his queen. A yagya is performed for a child,

68
00:03:21,974 --> 00:03:25,520
then Ram is born. There is no kidnapping at sea in between.

69
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,692
Now the Uttara Kanda. This is the last part,

70
00:03:28,692 --> 00:03:33,225
where Ravan's own story also comes. His birth,

71
00:03:33,225 --> 00:03:38,210
his penance, his boons. The clue should have been found here.

72
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:42,271
But here too the story of Kaushalya's box is not found,

73
00:03:42,271 --> 00:03:46,331
so scholars say. So where did this story come from?

74
00:03:46,331 --> 00:03:49,580
The answer lies hidden in the history of Ananda Ramayan.

75
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:53,677
There are other versions of the Ram story too. There is the Adhyatma Ramayan,

76
00:03:53,677 --> 00:03:55,725
there is Kamban's Tamil Ramayan.

77
00:03:55,725 --> 00:04:01,870
Our evidence shows this box episode clearly only in Ananda Ramayan.

78
00:04:01,870 --> 00:04:04,508
So the picture is clear so far.

79
00:04:04,508 --> 00:04:08,277
The real home of the viral story is Ananda Ramayan, not Valmiki.

80
00:04:08,277 --> 00:04:12,800
But don't people consider Ananda Ramayan too as Valmiki's?

81
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:17,524
Now the biggest question. Who wrote the Ananda Ramayan, and when?

82
00:04:17,524 --> 00:04:21,776
Here, tradition and historians give different answers.

83
00:04:21,776 --> 00:04:24,610
Tradition means beliefs handed down through generations.

84
00:04:24,610 --> 00:04:25,686
Tradition says,

85
00:04:25,686 --> 00:04:28,916
the Ananda Ramayan is also the work of Sage Valmiki.

86
00:04:28,916 --> 00:04:32,145
That is why many devotees consider it as sacred

87
00:04:32,145 --> 00:04:33,580
as the Valmiki Ramayan.

88
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:37,445
Now to the historians. Text historians are the people

89
00:04:37,445 --> 00:04:41,697
who judge a book's age from its language and style.

90
00:04:41,697 --> 00:04:43,630
Their opinion is completely different.

91
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:45,839
Most modern scholars say,

92
00:04:45,839 --> 00:04:49,373
the Ananda Ramayan was written in the 15th century CE,

93
00:04:49,373 --> 00:04:54,233
that is, around the period of 1500. It is a medieval book,

94
00:04:54,233 --> 00:04:56,000
medieval means the Middle Ages.

95
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,112
So it is clear.

96
00:04:57,112 --> 00:05:00,820
According to scholars, this is not Valmiki's original work,

97
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:03,415
but a work written later.

98
00:05:03,415 --> 00:05:06,010
And it is the one that tells the story of the box.

99
00:05:06,010 --> 00:05:09,343
Then why was this book written? Scholars say,

100
00:05:09,343 --> 00:05:11,565
its special feature is the new stories.

101
00:05:11,565 --> 00:05:16,380
Stories that give the Valmiki Ramayan story a background from before.

102
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:18,542
Like a prequel of a film.

103
00:05:18,542 --> 00:05:20,704
You already know the main story,

104
00:05:20,704 --> 00:05:23,587
the prequel tells what happened before that.

105
00:05:23,587 --> 00:05:26,470
Kaushalya's box seems just like that kind of prequel.

106
00:05:26,470 --> 00:05:28,643
But the devotees' question is also fair.

107
00:05:28,643 --> 00:05:30,505
Were these stories completely new,

108
00:05:30,505 --> 00:05:33,608
or were they already on people's lips,

109
00:05:33,608 --> 00:05:35,160
and written down later?

110
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:38,103
This is the real debate. Some say,

111
00:05:38,103 --> 00:05:41,465
it is an old oral tradition, oral means spoken,

112
00:05:41,465 --> 00:05:44,408
which was only told aloud. Others say,

113
00:05:44,408 --> 00:05:46,930
it is a later creative imagination.

114
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:50,215
Deciding who is right is not our job.

115
00:05:50,215 --> 00:05:54,230
We only keep the evidence. But in the structure of this story,

116
00:05:54,230 --> 00:05:56,420
an even bigger clue is hidden.

117
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:59,870
Now listen carefully. The king gets a prophecy,

118
00:05:59,870 --> 00:06:02,285
that the child to be born will cause his death.

119
00:06:02,285 --> 00:06:05,390
Have you heard this story somewhere else before?

120
00:06:05,390 --> 00:06:08,825
Yes, in the Bhagavata Purana. There Kamsa finds out,

121
00:06:08,825 --> 00:06:11,229
that Devaki's son will bring about his end.

122
00:06:11,229 --> 00:06:14,320
And Kamsa throws Devaki into prison.

123
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:17,879
Now place the stories side by side. A frightened king, a prophecy,

124
00:06:17,879 --> 00:06:22,228
and the imprisonment of the mother-to-be. The structure is almost the same,

125
00:06:22,228 --> 00:06:23,810
only the names have changed.

126
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:27,599
Folklorists, that is, experts on folk tales, call this a motif.

127
00:06:27,599 --> 00:06:29,873
A motif means a story pattern

128
00:06:29,873 --> 00:06:32,904
that travels from tale to tale,

129
00:06:32,904 --> 00:06:34,420
like the tune of a song.

130
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:37,810
Their view is that the pattern of Kaushalya's abduction

131
00:06:37,810 --> 00:06:42,048
may have been inspired by the story of Kamsa and Devaki.

132
00:06:42,048 --> 00:06:44,590
Inspired means made by taking inspiration from it.

133
00:06:44,590 --> 00:06:48,783
But understand this too, stories resembling each other is no insult.

134
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:52,595
In India, stories have always spoken to one another,

135
00:06:52,595 --> 00:06:54,120
from village to village.

136
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:56,090
Grandmothers too, while telling a story,

137
00:06:56,090 --> 00:06:58,718
would add new color to an old tale.

138
00:06:58,718 --> 00:07:02,330
Perhaps the writers of the texts did something similar.

139
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:05,122
But texts are just a matter of paper.

140
00:07:05,122 --> 00:07:07,516
The real question begins now.

141
00:07:07,516 --> 00:07:09,909
Is there any proof from beneath the ground too,

142
00:07:09,909 --> 00:07:13,100
of Kaushalya's Kosala?

143
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:16,161
Now the books are closed, and the spade is in hand.

144
00:07:16,161 --> 00:07:18,348
A spade means a digging tool.

145
00:07:18,348 --> 00:07:23,595
Archaeology is the science of digging the earth to find traces of ancient people.

146
00:07:23,595 --> 00:07:24,470
Let's go to Ayodhya.

147
00:07:24,470 --> 00:07:26,232
In the 1975 season,

148
00:07:26,232 --> 00:07:30,195
a project called Archaeology of Ramayana Sites reached Ayodhya.

149
00:07:30,195 --> 00:07:31,516
The aim was simple.

150
00:07:31,516 --> 00:07:35,920
What lies hidden in the soil of places connected to the Ramayana?

151
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:39,172
This work was done under an ASI project.

152
00:07:39,172 --> 00:07:43,238
ASI means the Archaeological Survey of India, the country's archaeology organization.

153
00:07:43,238 --> 00:07:46,490
They dug the ground layer by layer.

154
00:07:46,490 --> 00:07:49,674
Layer means tah. Like the layers of a cake,

155
00:07:49,674 --> 00:07:51,089
the bottom one is the oldest.

156
00:07:51,089 --> 00:07:54,980
The earth too is formed by stacking layers of centuries.

157
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:58,776
And what was found at the very bottom? Continuous traces of human settlement,

158
00:07:58,776 --> 00:08:01,434
going back to the 7th century BCE.

159
00:08:01,434 --> 00:08:05,230
BCE means the time before the birth of Christ.

160
00:08:05,230 --> 00:08:09,037
Settlement means people lived here, built houses,

161
00:08:09,037 --> 00:08:11,153
They lived everyday lives.

162
00:08:11,153 --> 00:08:14,960
The layers of soil bear witness that people lived here.

163
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:18,667
But note this. The excavation tells us there was an old settlement.

164
00:08:18,667 --> 00:08:22,746
It doesn't tell us that Kaushalya was shut inside a box.

165
00:08:22,746 --> 00:08:24,970
The soil does not prove the legend.

166
00:08:24,970 --> 00:08:27,741
And it doesn't disprove it either.

167
00:08:27,741 --> 00:08:31,305
The legend and the excavation answer different questions.

168
00:08:31,305 --> 00:08:35,660
But the story of Kosala is not limited to Ayodhya. Let's move on.

169
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:37,979
Now Shravasti, the old capital of Kosala.

170
00:08:37,979 --> 00:08:40,685
In the Ramayan, Dasharath is the king of Kosala.

171
00:08:40,685 --> 00:08:44,164
Kosala means the large kingdom around Ayodhya,

172
00:08:44,164 --> 00:08:46,870
which was in today's Uttar Pradesh.

173
00:08:46,870 --> 00:08:49,603
Here, the ASI excavation found fortifications.

174
00:08:49,603 --> 00:08:53,117
Fortifications means the wall and enclosure that protected the city.

175
00:08:53,117 --> 00:08:56,240
Layers of a city settlement were found along with them.

176
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:59,709
These layers begin from the 6th century BCE.

177
00:08:59,709 --> 00:09:02,021
That means city life in Kosala

178
00:09:02,021 --> 00:09:05,490
was flourishing many centuries before Christ.

179
00:09:05,490 --> 00:09:09,597
So what does the soil say? There were old cities in Kosala,

180
00:09:09,597 --> 00:09:14,116
there were people, there were walls. But a box placed on an island in the sea,

181
00:09:14,116 --> 00:09:16,580
there is no excavation evidence for that.

182
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:17,732
And honestly,

183
00:09:17,732 --> 00:09:21,573
it is hard to find such evidence for any legend.

184
00:09:21,573 --> 00:09:25,030
How would a wooden box survive for centuries in the waves?

185
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:26,950
But the question is still there.

186
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:30,510
Now the part that no viral clip tells you.

187
00:09:30,510 --> 00:09:34,862
Is nothing known yet? The answer is, quite a lot.

188
00:09:34,862 --> 00:09:36,840
And that is the most interesting part.

189
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:41,515
Here is the biggest mystery. Before it was written in Sanskrit,

190
00:09:41,515 --> 00:09:45,340
where was this box legend born? In which region,

191
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:47,890
in which language, on whose tongue?

192
00:09:47,890 --> 00:09:52,418
It may have been a folk tale in some regional language.

193
00:09:52,418 --> 00:09:55,813
Regional means the own language of a particular area. But which one,

194
00:09:55,813 --> 00:09:57,700
nobody knows yet.

195
00:09:57,700 --> 00:10:01,187
The next mystery: who was the real author of the Ananda Ramayan?

196
00:10:01,187 --> 00:10:02,931
Tradition says Valmiki,

197
00:10:02,931 --> 00:10:06,854
scholars speak of some later author.

198
00:10:06,854 --> 00:10:09,470
The exact identity is still unclear.

199
00:10:09,470 --> 00:10:11,457
The last question is the deepest.

200
00:10:11,457 --> 00:10:16,224
Is this story the surviving echo of some ancient oral tradition?

201
00:10:16,224 --> 00:10:19,800
Or the poet's own imagination? The debate is still open.

202
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:22,233
So now you have the full picture.

203
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:25,362
The story is in the Ananda Ramayan. It's not found in Valmiki.

204
00:10:25,362 --> 00:10:28,490
And its roots are still being searched for.

205
00:10:28,490 --> 00:10:32,470
If you want to see this world yourself, go to Ayodhya.

206
00:10:32,470 --> 00:10:35,364
Watch the evening aarti on the banks of the Saryu.

207
00:10:35,364 --> 00:10:38,620
The same river the Ramayan mentions again and again.

208
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:39,874
Then go to Shravasti.

209
00:10:39,874 --> 00:10:43,636
There you can see old mounds and ruins out in the open.

210
00:10:43,636 --> 00:10:45,726
A mound means a raised heap of earth,

211
00:10:45,726 --> 00:10:49,070
with a settlement centuries old buried beneath it.

212
00:10:49,070 --> 00:10:50,592
And if you want to read the texts,

213
00:10:50,592 --> 00:10:55,156
read the Bala Kanda of Valmiki Ramayan and the Sara Kanda of Ananda Ramayan

214
00:10:55,156 --> 00:10:58,960
side by side. You'll spot the difference yourself.

215
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:01,203
And ask your grandmother at home.

216
00:11:01,203 --> 00:11:04,407
Where did she hear this box story? Who knows,

217
00:11:04,407 --> 00:11:07,290
maybe some old regional version is hidden in her memory.

218
00:11:07,290 --> 00:11:10,228
So, back to where we started.

219
00:11:10,228 --> 00:11:14,268
Did Ravan imprison Ram's mother in the sea?

220
00:11:14,268 --> 00:11:17,940
Ananda Ramayan says yes. Valmiki is silent on this.

221
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:21,143
Scholars consider it a 15th century work,

222
00:11:21,143 --> 00:11:23,946
with an echo of Kamsa's story.

223
00:11:23,946 --> 00:11:28,350
Tradition credits it to Valmiki. The judgment is up to you.

224
00:11:28,350 --> 00:11:31,396
Our next journey is to the sea. Ram Setu,

225
00:11:31,396 --> 00:11:35,964
which ISRO's satellite map showed as a 29 km long

226
00:11:35,964 --> 00:11:41,040
chain of rocks under the water. But how was it made?

227
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:45,578
The Geological Survey of India considers it a natural formation shaped by waves.

228
00:11:45,578 --> 00:11:48,981
Some people say it's the work of human hands.

229
00:11:48,981 --> 00:11:51,250
What's the truth? In the next video.

230
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:54,150
And now a question for you.

231
00:11:54,150 --> 00:12:01,399
Where did you first hear this box story,

232
00:12:01,399 --> 00:12:08,648
from your grandmother, or on your phone? Do tell us in the comments.
